  "header": {
    "subsystemType": "Hrot.Scenario",
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "basic-desert",
    "description": "What: Temperament & Stress \u00a76 (CE-2272, R-2034) - on open basic-desert two fire teams of four hold their spots facing south (CombatPosture, stay, a post; ROE StayOnTask): 'Regular 1-4' (Friend riflemen, the default temperament - obedience 0.8, nerve 0.5) at x 270-274.5 and 'Militia 1-4' (Friend riflemen, obedience 0.3, nerve 0.3) at x 340-344.5, y 300. Each is under the SAME fire: 'Gunner Regular' / 'Gunner Militia' (Hostile automatic riflemen, InertSop) 120 m south (inside a rifleman's 150 m sight) fire 40 rounds, one every 1.3 s, at a point 10 m behind the team, 4 m up - every round passes over the team's heads (near misses, no hits). All immortal. Judge (100 s): (1) no regular breaks and the regulars fire back; (2) at least half the militia break (the Break reaction - down, no fire); (3) every man who broke recovers once the fire stops and is back on his task by the end; (4) printed per man: his peak stress, when he broke and recovered. Check: python3 scripts/utility-demo-check.py --launch ts-fire-discipline. \ud83d\udcc4 docs/DESIGN_Temperament_And_Stress.md \u00a76"
  },
